refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public voidDom\Element::insertAdjacentHTML Dom\AdjacentPositionwhere stringstring
Parses string as a fragment and inserts the resulting nodes at the position given by where, relative to this element. The fragment is parsed as HTML in an HTML document, and as XML in an XML document.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws a DOMException with code Dom\NO_MODIFICATION_ALLOWED_ERR if where is Dom\AdjacentPosition::BeforeBegin or Dom\AdjacentPosition::AfterEnd and this element has no parent, or its parent is the document.
Throws a DOMException with code Dom\SYNTAX_ERR if this element is in an XML document and string is not a well-formed XML fragment.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Dom\Element::insertAdjacentHTML example


<?php

$dom = Dom\HTMLDocument::createFromString(
    '<!DOCTYPE html><body><ul id="list"><li>Two</li></ul></body>',
    LIBXML_NOERROR
);

$list = $dom->getElementById('list');

$list->firstElementChild->insertAdjacentHTML(
    Dom\AdjacentPosition::BeforeBegin,
    '<li>One</li>'
);
$list->insertAdjacentHTML(
    Dom\AdjacentPosition::BeforeEnd,
    '<li>Three</li><li><b>Four</b></li>'
);

echo $list->outerHTML, "\n";


   &example.outputs;


<ul id="list"><li>One</li><li>Two</li><li>Three</li><li><b>Four</b></li></ul>
